fact WorkItem(id: "WI-330", description: some(value: "WI-307 phase 5: migrate typing_pass_spec onto row unification (proposal 045 §Phase 5). The reflect-side typing pass (stdlib/anthill/reflect/typing_pass_spec.anthill) declares effect handling that — until v1a — was a stub: effects were modeled as List[Type] with positional checks at the typer (typing.rs:6303). With v1a's unify_effect_rows live (commit 1d62e7a), the spec can honestly describe the algorithm. PIECES: (a) audit typing_pass_spec for effect-related operations and update their bodies to reflect row unification semantics (handler discharge, propagation of open tails, lacks-constraint accumulation once v1b lands); (b) replace positional 'actual ⊆ expected' rules with row-equivalence rules consulting effects_rows + EffectExpression algebra; (c) for the migrated stdlib Function/Stream/Collection/Iteration (post-WI-320 commit fae2516), thread the EffectsRuntime[Effects = E] requirement through the spec so the typer cross-checks against the auto-emitted requires that ship with each operation; (d) test that typing_pass_spec.anthill loads cleanly with the new shape and a sample operation type-checks via the spec — this is the proposal 013 deferred 'effect checking is honest now' acceptance criterion. SCOPE: spec stdlib file + integration tests that exercise the spec on the post-WI-307 typer. Depends on v1a (WI-307) shipped, ideally v1b (WI-328) and handler discharge (WI-329) too for full coverage. Completes proposal 013's deferred effect-checking."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-307", "WI-328", "WI-329"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
